  "notes": "Coordinates from the board's FRONT-LEFT corner seen from the top: x along the finger (0 = front/camera edge, board_length = back/antenna edge), y across the finger (0 = left edge where the switch is). Module ESP32-S3-MINI-1U 15.4x15.4x2.4 with its u.FL end flush with the back edge; keep 5 mm behind the back edge free of metal, cell and LRA, and route the flex antenna down the back wall. top_max_height is the mated u.FL plug (2.9), the module shield is 2.4 (the lid may be lower over the front strip, x < 11.1: tallest part there is FPC1 at 2.0). Bottom parts max 1.15 (SOT-23/VSSOP) - allow >= 0.35 clearance to the cell. Mic MK1 is a bottom-port part mounted on the BOTTOM side at mic_xy; its 0.6 mm port goes through the board, so the lid needs a ~0.8 mm hole straight above mic_xy. LED D1 is on top at led_xy under a 1.0-1.5 mm thinned window (~3 mm). Switch SW1 body 3.0x2.5x1.2 on the top side, plunger pointing out of the left edge at x = switch_offset; wall slot ~3.2 x 1.5 centred z = board_top+0.6. Touch pad 3x4 copper on top at touchpad_xy (needs only a thin, non-conductive lid: <= 1.0 mm there or an opening). FPC connector FPC1 on top at x 0.5-4.5 spanning y 1-17, FPC enters from the front edge; the camera head sits in a pod in front of the board (see stackup.svg / pod_mm). Wire pads for the cell (J1), charging pads (PAD1/2), LRA (M1), piezo (BZ1) and aux (J2) are all on the BOTTOM side, so the wire channel into the band should open under the board near x 12-20 (left) and x 15-18 (right).",
